tgd web design prototype
========================

A clickable React prototype of the reworked web UI, in the "Console"
design direction (sidebar, dense tables, light and dark themes, usable
on phones). It is a design aid only: all data is synthetic (src/data,
generated from fixed seeds), nothing talks to the backend, and none of
it is built into the web image.

Run it with Docker (nothing else needed on the host):

    cd web/mockup
    ./dev npm ci
    ./dev up

then open http://127.0.0.1:51737/ (MOCKUP_PORT changes the port);
./dev down stops it. ./dev shoot <outdir> <path>... takes screenshots
in light and dark, at desktop and phone width, through a Playwright
container, and ./dev click screenshots a dialog or tab after clicking
through it; TGD_AS=1, 3 or 5 views the mockup as a superadmin, a
restricted admin or a member. Running `npm ci` and `npm run dev`
directly also works where Node is installed.

Screens live at the same paths the production server answers (/users,
/users/<id>/history, /groups/<id>/chat, ...), never behind a fragment,
because the production pages will be server-rendered from those URLs.
List state (search, filters, sort, page) is kept in the query string.
Fonts are bundled from npm (@fontsource), so nothing is fetched from a
CDN at runtime.

Layout:

  src/data/    synthetic data per entity, and the query helper
  src/ui/      shell, table, filter bar, timeline and small parts
  src/pages/   one module per page
  src/styles/  stylesheets
  scripts/     screenshot scripts run by ./dev
